/**
  @page examples-pdes-index Partial differential equations
  @brief Guided solves from scalar diffusion to coupled systems.

  Start with @ref examples-pdes-poisson "Poisson". It introduces the full
  sequence of mesh creation, weak formulation, linear solution, and visualization.
  The remaining tutorials extend one or more parts of that sequence.

  | Tutorial | Main idea |
  | :--- | :--- |
  | @subpage examples-pdes-poisson | Scalar diffusion and homogeneous Dirichlet data |
  | @subpage examples-pdes-dg-poisson | Discontinuous affine space, SIPG fluxes and convergence checks |
  | @subpage examples-pdes-elasticity | Vector displacement and boundary traction |
  | @subpage examples-pdes-helmholtz | Wave propagation and complex-valued fields |
  | @subpage examples-pdes-stokes | Incompressibility, mixed spaces, and pressure normalization |
  | @subpage examples-pdes-navierstokes | Coupled velocity and pressure |
  | @subpage examples-pdes-periodic | Periodic boundary identification |
  | @subpage examples-pdes-surfacemesh | Differential operators on an embedded surface |

  For the derivation of the forms, see @ref guides-weak-formulations.
  For solver requirements, see @ref guides-solvers.

  @m_footernavigation
*/
